  "releaseNotes": "* Improved ``UserCredential`` equality checking in Equals methods\n* Improved ``ProcessResourcePolicy`` equality checking in Equals methods\n* Reduced default Timeout Threshold from 10 minutes to 2 minutes - This is probably close to as sane of a default Timeout Threshold as CliInvoke can provide without advanced knowledge of what program is being run. Users can easily specify a different Timeout Treshold with ``ProcessTimeoutPolicy.FromTimeSpan(TimeSpan)`` or ``new ProcessExitConfiguration(TimeSpan)` or use no timeout with ``ProcessTimeoutPolicy.None`` or ``new ProcessExitConfiguration(ProcessTimeoutPolicy.None)``. If you'd like to give feedback on this (or frankly any other aspect of CliInvoke), feel free to [create a discussion](https://github.com/alastairlundy/CliInvoke/discussions)",
